    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d937-a2">

                <pb facs="1093" n="997" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg997"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lord Salisbury to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: With reference to my note of
                    the 6th instant, I have the honor to transmit to your excellency translation of
                    a letter which the Spanish minister for foreign affairs has addressed to Her
                    Majesty’s ambassador at Madrid, explaining the difficulty in the way of bringing
                    home the sailors detained as prisoners of war at Portsmouth, N. H.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. H. Sanderson.</hi></signed><lb/>(In
                    the absence of the Marquis of Salisbury.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
